{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.ManifoldVolumePositive","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ManifoldVolumePositive","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.BlochWignerPositive","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.ManifoldVolumeBridge"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.ManifoldVolumePositive.vol_ne_zero_of_realises","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ManifoldVolumePositive.vol_ne_zero_of_realises","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ManifoldVolumePositive.lean#L65-L70","doc":"**The volume of such a manifold is nonzero**, hence the realisation is not\ndegenerate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.ManifoldVolumePositive.vol_pos_of_realises","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ManifoldVolumePositive.vol_pos_of_realises","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ManifoldVolumePositive.lean#L52-L63","doc":"**A manifold realised by a nonempty ideal triangulation has strictly positive\nvolume.**\n\nThe general form of `Encounter.FigureEightVolumeBridge.vol_pos_of_realises` and\n`Encounter.FiveTwoVolumeBridge.vol_pos_of_realises`, which reached the same conclusion at\ntheir own two shapes through a Clausen special value and through a volume comparison\nrespectively.  Neither route generalised; this one does not need either. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.ManifoldVolumePositive.triangulation_volume_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ManifoldVolumePositive.triangulation_volume_pos","kind":"theorem","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ManifoldVolumePositive.lean#L40-L50","doc":"**A nonempty ideal triangulation has strictly positive volume.**\n\nEach tetrahedron contributes strictly positively (`BlochWignerPositive.volume_pos`), and\n`0 < n` makes the index set nonempty — without which the sum is empty and the volume is\n`0`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}